                     /GO_process="GO:0042026 - protein refolding [Evidence
                     IEA]"
                     /note="60 kDa chaperone family; promotes refolding of
                     misfolded polypeptides especially under stressful
                     conditions; forms two stacked rings of heptamers to form a
                     barrel-shaped 14mer; ends can be capped by GroES;
                     misfolded proteins enter the barrel where they are
                     refolded when GroES binds; 60 kDa chaperone family;
                     promotes refolding of misfolded polypeptides especially
                     under stressful conditions; forms two stacked rings of
                     heptamers to form a barrel-shaped 14mer; ends can be
                     capped by GroES; misfolded proteins enter the barrel where
                     they are refolded when GroES binds; Derived by automated
                     computational analysis using gene prediction method:
                     Protein Homology."
